# === Privacy hard-guard (defense in depth) ===
# The public edition must NEVER contain patient-specific or individual-linking data.
# These patterns are excluded belt-and-suspenders, even though such files are not
# authored into this repository in the first place (the private N-of-1 overlay is
# kept entirely outside this repo).
_qa/
files/
backup/
staging/

# Page-adjudication crops. A crop of a printed page reproduces the author's characters —
# which is exactly what makes it evidence, and exactly why it cannot be redistributed. The
# articles adjudicated so far carry all-rights-reserved notices and no open deposit. What
# ships instead is `adjudications.json` beside each set: source-PDF digest, page, crop
# rectangle, dpi and the SHA-256 of the image. `regenerate_adjudications.py` turns that back
# into the identical bytes from a copy of the article the reader already holds, so the
# verification is unchanged and nothing copyrighted is republished. Same rule as `files/`
# above: publish the derivation, not the derived.
disease-models/*/research/page_adjudications/**/*.png
disease-models/*/research/page_adjudications/**/*.jpg
disease-models/*/research/page_adjudications/**/*.jpeg
disease-models/*/research/page_adjudications/**/*.tif
disease-models/*/research/page_adjudications/**/*.tiff
tmp/
overlay/
*private*
*patient*
*_clinical_*
*_overlay_*

# "Proband" may be used in public, disease-level methodology. Do not ignore it
# by name: semantic case linkage is enforced by the release gate instead.

# === Grant applications (never published) ===
# Working dossiers for research-funding calls: named individuals, contact
# details, organisation IDs, budget figures and draft form answers. Kept in the
# working tree so each new call reuses the accumulated context, excluded from
# the published repository by design.
grants/

# === Laboratory runtime instance (never published) ===
# The deployment profile splits into a portable half, tracked, and a local half that
# belongs to one machine and one moment: absolute paths, a runtime instance id, and the
# session references currently live. Both halves have a reason to stay out of the
# published repository — an absolute path breaks the clone-and-run portability that the
# profile exists to protect, and a machine path carries a username while a session ref
# carries a runtime identifier. The release gate looks for patient re-identification, not
# for either of those, so the exclusion is structural rather than a reminder to be careful.
deployment/local_instance.md

# === Standard ===
.DS_Store
*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
.env

# Optional molecular-dynamics runs are large, generated and non-canonical.
md-output/
*.dcd
state.tsv

# Per-session git worktrees. Ten interactive sessions have run against this single
# checkout, sharing one HEAD, one index and one working tree — so a branch created by
# one of them silently redirected another's commit, and a checkout by any of them
# would rewrite files the others had open. Isolating each session in its own worktree
# fixes that at the root, and the worktree directories are checkouts of this same
# repository: they must never be added back into it.
.claude/worktrees/

# Browser-automation session artefacts. Retrieval via a real browser (publisher
# bot-blocks) drops page snapshots, console logs and network traces here. They
# are transient, they record the URLs a session visited, and they have no place
# in a public repository — the retrieval outcome belongs in
# files/fulltext/_retrieval_manifest.jsonl and the handoff card instead.
.playwright-mcp/
